# The midnight turn (playtest 2, M41; stub — X13 fills it): after a lead-in in year 1 Stormbloom, a night card each
# on-campus month, first in the midnight slot (after every night card), so going out leads straight to the pick. "Go out" opens the midnight pick (`visit midnight`); six places are open then. Going out in term
# queues `night_suspicion` at 33%, and risky outcomes queue it at their own odds (I4); two copies bring at most one
# card the next morning (or the first month back on campus), the only way to a lockout. The cards never say whether
# you were seen.

@event night_lead_in
title: An Unsigned Note
trigger: auto
when: year == 1 and month == 7 and not off_campus
class: story
tone: eerie
art: map
tags: mystery
scene: A folded note slipped under a dormitory door at night, unsigned, a tiny silver map drawn in one corner.
text: A note under your door, unsigned: "The castle has a second timetable. It starts at midnight. Curfew is a suggestion made by people who go to bed early." In the corner, a map no bigger than a thumbnail, showing six doors that are open when they shouldn't be.
> left: Burn it
  flag night_unlocked
  find lead_second_timetable
  say: You hold it to the candle. The map in the corner is the last thing to burn, and you could swear it rearranged itself first.
> right: Keep it
  flag night_unlocked
  find lead_second_timetable
  guile +tiny
  say: You fold it into your book. Some nights you take it out and look at the six doors.

@event night_out
title: After Curfew
trigger: auto
slot: midnight
when: flag(night_unlocked) and not off_campus and not has(locked_out) and turn < max_turns
repeat: 1
class: story
tone: eerie
art: moon
tags: mystery
scene: A dormitory window at midnight, the castle dark beyond it, one lantern moving along a far battlement.
text: {month == 12: Starfall is close, and the sky over the towers is already restless.|{month == 4 or month == 10: Exams soon. Half the windows on your corridor are still lit.|{season == "winter": {~Frost on the window, and the corridors are colder than the snow.|Snow on the sills; the tower creaks like a ship.|Ice in the water jug, and the tower silent with snow.}|{season == "summer": {~The night is warm and the castle's windows are all open.|Moths at the window, and somebody laughing on the lawn.|The night is short and never quite dark.}|{~The castle settles for the night, beam by beam.|Rain on the leads, and a gargoyle gargling it.|The wind finds every keyhole in the tower.}}}}} {has(watched): Bram does his rounds earlier these nights. You've learned the sound of his boots.|{health < 30: Every bone you own would like to stay in bed.|{mood < 25: You can't sleep anyway.|{gold < 10: Your purse is light, and some doors after midnight pay.|{bonds(partner) > 0: {~A note under your door, in a hand you know: "Roof?"|You could be on the observatory roof with someone right now.|Somewhere across the castle, someone you love is also awake.}|{final_year: {~Your last year. The castle at night won't be yours much longer.|The doors you know by heart will open for someone else next year.|Next year someone else will lie awake in this bed.}|{~Somewhere a door that should be locked isn't.|Down in the courtyard, a lantern goes out on purpose.|Someone has left the servants' stair unbolted again.}}}}}}}
> left: Sleep
  say: {~You blow out the candle and let the castle keep its secrets for one more night.|Sleep. The night can wait. It always does.|You pull the blanket up and listen to the castle until you're asleep.}
> right: Go out
  mood -small
  health -small
  visit midnight
  if term:
    queue night_suspicion chance unlikely
  say: {~You wait for the last footsteps to fade, then ease the door open.|Boots in hand, you take the servants' stair.|You slip out while the castle is still settling, and nobody hears.}

# The morning after you were noticed (queued by the night's cards, I4): the only source of lockouts.
@event night_suspicion
title: A Word in the Morning
trigger: queued
slot: morning
# Caught in a term's last month and off home or to an internship (I6): it waits until you're back on campus.
defer: off_campus
repeat: 1
class: incident
tone: tense
art: eye
tags: crisis
scene: A prefect waiting at the foot of a dormitory stair at breakfast time, arms folded, a small notebook open.
text: {has(watched): Bram is waiting at the foot of the stair, and this time he has a notebook open. "Twice," he says. "I did warn you."|Bram is waiting at the foot of the stair. "Someone was out last night," he says, looking at nobody in particular, which is to say at you.}
> left: Deny everything
  guile +tiny
  if has(watched):
    lose watched
    gain locked_out
    gain detention 3
    mood -medium
    say: Three months of detention and a door that is checked at midnight. Bram writes it all down, neatly.
  else:
    gain watched
    say: "I'll be keeping an eye on you." He means it literally.
> right: Own up
  alignment +tiny
  if has(watched):
    lose watched
    gain locked_out
    gain detention 3
    mood -medium
    say: Three months of detention and a door that is checked at midnight. Bram writes it all down, neatly.
  else:
    gain watched
    say: "I'll be keeping an eye on you." He means it literally.

# ---------------- One night at each open place (X13 adds more) ----------------

@event midnight_newt_cards
title: Upstairs at the Newt
place: gilded_newt
slot: midnight
# Retired (feedback 2026-10-16): the Newt's nights are the company offer, then the high table (`@place always:`).
when: false
class: routine
tone: tense
repeat: 2
weight: 10
art: cup
tags: money danger
scene: A smoky upstairs room at a tavern after hours, a card table under one lamp, coins stacked high.
text: Upstairs at the Gilded Newt, after hours, the real game starts. The stakes are higher than anything downstairs, and nobody asks your name.
> left: Play a few hands
  alignment -tiny
  gold -medium
  challenge deceive adept- unlikely luck:
    win:
      gold +large
      gold +medium
      say: {~You leave with more than you came with and a few new enemies who smile too much.|Luck, nerve and one well-timed sigh. The pot is yours.}
    lose:
      queue night_suspicion chance even
      say: {~The cards go cold, and so does your purse. On the stair down, a face from the castle turns away a little too fast.|You lose your stake and walk back in the dark, poorer, wiser and not sure you went unseen.}
> right: Watch, then leave
  say: {~You watch one hand, see someone lose a familiar on a bluff, and leave before you're tempted.|You stay long enough to learn the rules, and leave before they learn you.}

@event midnight_boathouse_ring
title: The Ring Under the Boathouse
place: boathouse
slot: midnight
class: routine
tone: tense
# The ring (feedback 2026-10-16): one of the two entry cards opens every boathouse night (`@place always:`). A win
# leads to the next bout (ring_bout_2 … 4), each harder and better paid. Some nights the house runs last-standing
# rules, rolled when the card is drawn and said before you choose: once you step in, you fight until you lose or
# have won four. Declining sends you to the side bets.
repeat: 2
weight: 10
art: sword
tags: danger money
scene: A cellar under a boathouse, lanterns hung from the beams, students in a ring around two duellists, coins changing hands.
on_show:
  unflag ring_last_standing
  chance unlikely:
    flag ring_last_standing
text: {Under the boathouse, by lantern light, someone has chalked a ring on the flagstones. Purses go to whoever is still standing.|The chalk ring under the boathouse again, freshly drawn. The student holding the money knows your face.|The ring is busier than ever, and the money-holder nods to you like a regular.} {flag(ring_last_standing): Tonight a slate by the steps reads LAST STANDING: whoever steps in fights until they drop or have beaten four.|"Next," says the student holding the money, looking at you. Win, and you can fight on for a bigger purse.}
> left: Step into the ring
  hint: Four bouts at most, each harder and richer.
  challenge combat adept-:
    win:
      gold +medium
      renown +tiny
      queue ring_bout_2 now
      say: {You win the first bout and the ring's respect, which is worth less and lasts longer.|Your opponent yields. Somebody whistles, and the money-holder looks at you: another?|You put your opponent down in the first exchange, and the crowd starts calling your name.}
    lose:
      unflag ring_last_standing
      health -medium
      queue night_suspicion chance even
      say: {You lose, and limp home past a window where a light is still burning.|A bruising loss, and a lantern somewhere on the path home. Maybe it saw you; maybe not.|You go down to a first-year with long arms. The crowd enjoys it more than you do.}
> right: Not tonight
  hint: Watch, and bet if you like.
  unflag ring_last_standing
  queue ring_side_bets now
  say: {You stay at the edge of the crowd and watch someone else's turn.|You shake your head. The money-holder shrugs and looks for somebody braver.|"Not tonight," you say, and find a place on the cellar steps to watch.}

@event midnight_kitchen_raid
title: The Kitchens at Midnight
place: refectory
slot: midnight
class: routine
tone: light
repeat: 2
weight: 10
art: meal
tags: danger
scene: A dark castle kitchen at midnight, a student with a candle reaching into a larder, a cat watching from the hearth.
text: The refectory kitchens at midnight: banked fires, a larder that isn't locked, and the smell of tomorrow's bread already rising.
> left: Fill your pockets
  alignment -tiny
  lose hungry
  health +small
  queue night_suspicion chance even
  say: {~Bread, cheese and half a pie. Nobody counts the pies, you hope, and the scullery door creaks as you leave.|You eat by the banked fire with the kitchen cat. On your way out, a kitchen boy is up early. Did he see you?}
> right: Just warm yourself by the fire
  mood +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~You sit by the embers until your hands stop hurting, and take nothing. The walk back is cold.|The kitchen cat sits with you. You leave the larder alone, feel strangely proud of it, and shiver all the way back to bed.}

@event midnight_restricted_stacks
title: The Restricted Stacks
place: restricted_section
slot: midnight
class: routine
tone: eerie
repeat: 2
weight: 10
art: book
tags: mystery danger
scene: A chained library section at midnight, a student reading by a stolen candle, shelves leaning in like listeners.
text: The Restricted Section at midnight. The chains on the shelves clink when nobody touches them. One book has been left open, as if for you.
> left: Read the open book
  challenge research apprentice+:
    win:
      lore +small
      say: {~Three pages before the book closes itself. You remember every word, which is worrying.|The book shows you a diagram you're not supposed to understand. You understand it.}
    lose:
      mood -small
      queue night_suspicion chance even
      say: {~The book slams shut and a lamp comes on two floors down. You're gone before it reaches the stair.|The pages scream, briefly. You leave quickly, and hope nobody heard.}
> right: Leave it open and go
  say: {~You back away from the book. It seems disappointed.|You leave it open for whoever it was waiting for. It wasn't you, you decide.}

@event midnight_observatory_stars
title: Stars at Midnight
place: observatory
slot: midnight
class: routine
tone: warm
repeat: 2
weight: 10
art: moon
tags: nature
scene: The observatory roof at midnight, a student lying on the leads, the sky thick with stars.
text: The observatory roof at midnight is the quietest place in the castle. {bonds(partner) > 0: You've brought someone.|The stars are very close tonight.} Nobody comes up here after curfew, mostly.
> left: Stay until the sky turns
  mood +medium
  health -small
  say: {~You count stars until you lose count, and then until the sky goes grey. You'll be tired. It was worth it.|A meteor, then another. You stay until the first bell.}
> right: An hour, then bed
  mood +small
  queue night_suspicion chance slim
  say: {~An hour of stars, and you're back in bed before anyone stirs, you think.|You slip back down the stair, the sky still in your eyes. A lantern turns a far corner, and you don't wait to see whose.}

@event midnight_passage_mapping
title: The Passage After Dark
place: gargoyle_passage
slot: midnight
class: routine
tone: eerie
repeat: 2
weight: 10
art: map
tags: club mystery
scene: A secret passage behind a gargoyle at midnight, chalk marks on the walls, a candle guttering in a draught from nowhere.
text: Behind the third gargoyle the passage is busier at midnight than at noon. {met(corvin): Corvin's chalk marks are fresh.|Someone's chalk marks are fresh.} A draught comes from a direction that has no wall.
> left: Follow the draught
  challenge research apprentice+:
    win:
      lore +small
      guile +tiny
      say: {~The draught leads you to a door you've never seen, and then, politely, closes it.|A new turning, a new stair. You chalk it for the map.}
    lose:
      health -small
      queue night_suspicion chance even
      say: {~After an hour of cold stone, the passage lets you out somewhere unexpected: the prefects' corridor, empty, you hope.|You get lost for an hour and come out in the wrong tower, cold and dusty, and not alone on the stair.}
> right: Mark it and go back
  say: {~You chalk an arrow at the turning and leave the rest for another night.|You mark it on your copy of the map and go back to bed, a little sorry.}
